	(text "J9: USB-C socket on the enclosure. P1: USB-C plug in U1's\nown USB-C socket. Wired straight through; no CC lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 44.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9260a140-aed6-4d1c-b1dc-899146b807cb")
	)
	(text "U1 is powered through its own USB-C socket, by P1.\n5VDC is its 5V pad, joined to the USB-C supply.\nPin numbers count the edge pads from 5V round the\nboard; the board prints only the GP names."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 91.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0342dfaa-ce09-4313-9ec4-921a0ac60e68")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.14 15.875 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "33a5ac9c-4e26-4af2-a659-62ed05397747")
	)
	(text "OLED DISPLAY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.05 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5bc2df12-0a7e-49a4-88f6-10c33d4d734d")
	)
	(text "SSD1306, 128 x 64, white."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 107.95 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "615cbc87-e453-4c27-b84f-7587eb9b05e0")
	)
	(text "RP2040-ZERO MICROCONTROLLER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.42 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "61eed9ba-0387-4745-9b10-42875fe97891")
	)
	(text "JST XH at U1's board only: headers J1 and J5 there,\nhousings J2 and J6 on the cables. At U2 and U3 the\ncables are soldered directly. Each end is drawn as built.\nWhich pin of each connector is pin 1 is not recorded.\nUSB-C extension J9 to P1: 5VDC, GND, USB_DP, USB_DM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6657592e-2a59-4c43-b266-38c56855be36")
	)
	(text "1. Power: only through the enclosure's USB-C socket\n   (J9), 5 V DC.\n2. Parts are through-hole on one perfboard: U1, BZ1\n   and its driver. U2 and U3 are cabled to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "793a51a6-9f36-486e-b782-29e74956c844")
	)
	(text "ROTARY ENCODER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 146.05 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a3b025be-cc5f-40e6-9270-8b371851a82d")
	)
	(text "Q1: find C, B, E with a tester before soldering;\nBC337 makers differ.\nR1: 100 Ω or more at 0.25 W, so that it survives\nBUZZER stuck high with Q1 on.\nD1: band (cathode) on BZ1's + lead."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd1d47ad-e8e4-4011-a62c-e8cd300bf16b")
	)
	(text "MAGNETIC BUZZER AND DRIVER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 58.42 105.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "be67d732-d620-401c-b65d-6a7948047a84")
	)
	(text "The module's own resistors pull CLK, DT and SW up to +."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 107.95 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c2e7fe98-fdba-4508-9b0b-a4f606445a50")
	)
